              "id": "ps-lsn-c2903f",
              "order": 3,
              "title": "Out into the world",
              "subtitle": "Everyday words for everyday adventures.",
              "objective": "Ask politely, apologise, ask what something means, and ask someone to repeat themselves - the four phrases that keep a conversation going when you do not understand.",
              "variety": "ps-var-yusufzai",
              "items": [
                {
                  "id": "ps-itm-68b3a5",
                  "native": "مهرباني وکړئ",
                  "romanisation": "Mehrbani wakray",
                  "meaning": "Please",
                  "context": "Ask for something politely.",
                  "usage_note": "Literally \"do a kindness\". Used before or after a request.",
